UNION combines the results of two or more SELECT statements and removes duplicate rows. 
UNION ALL also combines result sets but retains duplicates. Since UNION ALL does not perform duplicate elimination, it is generally faster than UNION.

UNION      = Unique rows only
UNION ALL  = All rows, including duplicates


| Feature                                | UNION | UNION ALL |
| -------------------------------------- | ----- | --------- |
| Combines multiple result sets          | ✅     | ✅         |
| Removes duplicates                     | ✅ Yes | ❌ No      |
| Returns only unique rows               | ✅     | ❌         |
| Faster                                 | ❌ No  | ✅ Yes     |
| Additional sorting/comparison required | ✅ Yes | ❌ No      |



